      "title": "SQL injection in user search",
      "description": "Search pastes the name query parameter into the SQL text with Sprintf. The value is not escaped or bound. Any caller of GET /users can read or change any row in the database with a crafted name. Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter instead of formatting it into the query.",
      "suggested_change": "\trows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search pastes the name query parameter into the SQL text with Sprintf. The value is not escaped or bound.",
      "consequence": "Any caller of GET /users can read or change any row in the database with a crafted name.",
      "fix": "Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter instead of formatting it into the query."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 63,
      "line_end": 63,
      "title": "Mutex stays locked on missing key",
      "description": "Count takes h.mu, then returns early when key is empty without unlocking it. One request without a key leaves the lock held, so every later GET /count request hangs forever. Validate key before taking the lock, or unlock with defer right after Lock.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:trailofbits.go.missing-unlock-before-return.missing-unlock-before-return",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
