      "line_number": 83,
      "line_end": 83,
      "title": "Nil response dereferenced on fetch error",
      "description": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil. Whenever the upstream is unreachable, GET /upstream panics instead of returning 502. Move the deferred Close below the error check.",
      "suggested_change": "\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\tdefer resp.Body.Close()",
